Define EM_SETCARETINDEX when the SDK headers lack it

EM_SETCARETINDEX is one of the edit-control messages Windows 10 added to
CommCtrl.h. mingw-w64's commctrl.h does not define it -- neither the headers
this was built with (mingw-w64-headers 14.0.0.r353) nor mingw-w64 master as
of 2026-09 -- so edit_control.cpp stops with

    'EM_SETCARETINDEX' was not declared in this scope

Define it when it is missing, as ECM_FIRST + 17, the value Wine's commctrl.h
gives it.

Upstream: not submitted yet; mingw-w64 is the better home for the define
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/src/windows/edit_control.cpp b/src/windows/edit_control.cpp
index 92b6b25..c86ea8b 100644
--- a/src/windows/edit_control.cpp
+++ b/src/windows/edit_control.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,10 @@
 #include <type_traits>
 #include <memory>
 
+#ifndef EM_SETCARETINDEX
+#define EM_SETCARETINDEX (ECM_FIRST + 17)
+#endif
+
 namespace WinLib {
 
     EditControl::EditControl() : isMultiLine(false), forwardArrowKeys(false), stopFowardingOnClick(false), autoExpand(false), hBuddy(NULL)
